    "title": "BVU names basketball court after alumnus - NewsBreak",
    "text": "STORM LAKE , Iowa ( KCAU ) — A northwest Iowa university named its basketball court in honor of one of its athletic hall of famers and long-time supporters. The court inside Sieben’s Fieldhouse will now be known as Saggau Family Court to honor the late Bernie Saggau, who died on May 10 at the age of 96. Story continues below The Denison, Iowa, native went to Buena Vista University back in 1945 and earned little All-American honors in football, along with winning championships in track and field. He graduated from BVU in 1949. Saggau was inducted into the university’s athletic hall of fame 20 years later. He served as the executive director for the Iowa High School Athletic Association for 38 years. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to SiouxlandProud | Sioux City, IA | News, Weather, and Sports.",
